<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shapur I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 241–272 CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century">3rd century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shapur I was the second king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sasanian-empire">Sasanian Empire</a>, who reigned from 241 to 272 CE. He defeated several Roman emperors, capturing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antioch">Antioch</a> and taking <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valerian">Emperor Valerian</a> prisoner at Edessa in 260 CE. Accounts of the Sasanian Empire also credit him with founding cities and using captured Roman engineers to build infrastructure.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/shapur-i.jpg" alt="Shapur I" width="208" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown after Rawlinson, George, 1812-1902 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Shapour_I_statue.gif" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
